NAME
    rotate - set the scene's rotation and redraw

SYNOPSIS
    rotate [x y z [px py pz]]

DESCRIPTION
    The geometry engine's record list survives between commands -- it IS
    the scene. Build one (tri, tri ... k, or cube's aftermath), then
    rotate it: this command rewrites only the engine's rotation matrix
    and redraws. Angles are in BRADS: 256 is a full turn, 64 is 90
    degrees, negative allowed. They apply as yaw (y), then pitch (x),
    then roll (z). WITHOUT a pivot the translation parameters are left
    alone: the model turns about its own origin and keeps its push-out
    -- right for origin-centred scenes like cube's (run cube, then
    rotate 0 32 0). WITH a pivot (px py pz) the whole transform is
    rewritten so the pivot maps to itself -- right for tri-built scenes
    whose depth is baked into the vertices (pivot on the scene's middle,
    0 0 400 say, and it turns in place). Bare rotate resets the rotation
    and keeps the translation. Needs the engine.

EXAMPLES
    cube 1
    rotate 0 16 0             yaw cube's model an eighth-turn in place
    tri -80 -80 300 80 -80 300 0 40 420 f 31 0 0
    rotate 0 32 0 0 0 360     yaw a tri scene about its middle
    rotate                    reset the rotation

SEE ALSO
    tri, cube, g3d
